#: src/macros/intro.md:6
msgid "What Is A Macro"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro.md:8
msgid ""
"Before looking at macros in detail, it is helpful to build a conceptual "
"model of what macros are and how they fit into the compilation pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro.md:11
msgid "At their core, macros are **meta-programming**:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro.md:13
msgid "They take input code (expressed as tokens) and emit output code."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro.md:14
msgid ""
"They execute during compilation, expanding before type checking and semantic "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro.md:16
msgid ""
"They allow expressing patterns and abstractions that cannot be written with "
"generics or standard functions."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro.md:19
msgid ""
"We will explore how compilers process source code, and how different macro "
"systems hook into this process."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/intro.md:25
msgid ""
"Ask students if they have used macros in other languages (e.g., C/C++ "
"preprocessor, Lisp, or Clojure)."
msgstr ""
